app.page.dangerousGoods.list1:
- explosive materials (EM);
- compressed, liquefied, and dissolved gases under pressure;
- flammable liquids (FL);
- flammable solids (FS) and self-igniting substances (SIS);
- substances that emit flammable gases when in contact with water;
- oxidizing substances (OX) and organic peroxides (OP);
- toxic (T) and infectious substances (IS);
- radioactive materials (RM);
- corrosive substances (CS);
- other dangerous substances.

app.page.dangerousGoods.list2:
- absolute vapor pressure at 50°C is equal to or greater than 3 kgf/cm² (300 kPa);
- critical temperature below 50°C. By physical state, gases are divided into:
- compressed gases with a critical temperature below -10°C;
- liquefied gases with a critical temperature equal to or above -10°C but below 70°C;
- liquefied gases with a critical temperature equal to or above 70°C;
- gases dissolved under pressure;
- liquefied by cooling;
- aerosols and compressed gases subject to special regulations. **Subclass 2.1** — non-flammable gases; **Subclass 2.2** — non-flammable toxic gases; **Subclass 2.3** — flammable gases; **Subclass 2.4** — toxic flammable gases; **Subclass 2.5** — chemically unstable; **Subclass 2.6** — chemically unstable toxic.

